        <div class="tab-content" id="tab-exports" data-main="exports" data-sub="files">
            <div class="info">
                The three inventory lists as <strong>Excel-safe CSV</strong> (UTF-8 with BOM, formula injection
                neutralised), each covering <strong>all devices</strong>, sorted column by column. Pick the file
                and open it - the download starts immediately and the URL is bookmarkable.
                <br><br>
                Want only <em>some</em> devices? Use the <strong>hardware</strong> / <strong>software</strong>
                buttons on MeshCentral's own device list toolbar: they export exactly the devices you ticked
                there, with the same columns and the same license values.
            </div>
            <div class="controls">
                <label for="exportType">Export file</label>
                <select id="exportType" class="filter-select">
                    <option value="hardware">Hardware inventory (group, host, OS, component, value, details)</option>
                    <option value="software">Software inventory (group, host, program, version, publisher, license)</option>
                    <option value="vulns" selected>Vulnerabilities (group, host, status, CVE, severity, rating, comment)</option>
                </select>
                <button id="exportGo" class="green" data-help="exp.go">Download CSV</button>
            </div>
            <h3>Direct links (bookmarkable)</h3>
            <div class="controls">
                <a href="/pluginadmin.ashx?pin={{shortName}}&amp;action=export&amp;type=hardware" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Hardware CSV</a>
                <a href="/pluginadmin.ashx?pin={{shortName}}&amp;action=export&amp;type=software" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Software CSV</a>
                <a href="/pluginadmin.ashx?pin={{shortName}}&amp;action=export&amp;type=vulns" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Vulnerabilities CSV</a>
            </div>
        </div>
